# Version bump

The product version is `[workspace.package] version` in `Cargo.toml`. The web health badge shows it as `v` plus `CARGO_PKG_VERSION`.

When a task changes project code, increase that patch number once before finishing (`0.1.1` → `0.1.2`). One bump per requested change, not once per file. Do not bump for a read-only answer.

A running `vigil.exe` keeps the version it was built with. After a bump, rebuild and restart so the badge matches.

After the version number changes, create a git commit with exactly this message, substituting the new number:

`update to vertsion X.Y.Z`

Do not push unless the user asks.
